WEBVTT

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.610
You've been keeping secrets 
from me, Sakamichi!

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:10.030
B-But, mom, I've explained it so many times.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.910
You took your bike all the way to Mt. Fuji!

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.160
Well, actually...

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.420
I heard you were going to Hakone,
but nobody told me you were going to Mt. Fuji!

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.660
What? I did tell you.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.790
Excuse me, ma'am. My name is Imaizumi.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.860
Excuse the intrusion. I'm Naruko.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.880
Written "cry" and "child," then "sentence" 
and "lucky," my name is Naruko Shoukichi.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.590
Onoda-kun did something super amazing.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.500
At the Inter-High, the year's biggest race...

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.260
Onoda-kun won the general classification!

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.480
He carried our wishes...

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.070
...to the finish line.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.390
What on earth is the Inter-High?

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.230
That's your question?

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.400
<i>This won't be easy.</i>

00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:00.200
Basically, he climbed Mt. Fuji faster 
than any other man in the country.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:02.620
That is amazing.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.410
<i>It worked.</i>

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.510
That's why you slept for 
three days after coming home.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:12.040
I was so exhausted, I couldn't move.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:13.130
Oh, right.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.220
Ma'am, we brought this.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.720
<b>Inter-High Winner
The Man Who Conquered Mt. Fuji
Onoda Sakamichi</b>

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.720
Onoda-kun's in a magazine.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:25.020
Oh, my. How cool.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.520
Look at this, Sakamichi. 
This is a nice photo.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.290
I'm good. I've already seen it.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.650
This is great.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:35.860
I forgot my camera in the car, so I 
didn't get to take a picture of you.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.810
You were there?!

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:39.680
You were there?!

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.390
Oh, didn't I tell you?

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:43.790
I was watching all through 
the award ceremony.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.510
You were watching, and you 
still don't understand?

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.460
Then that voice I heard then...

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.960
Do your best, Sakamichi!

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.460
Imaizumi-kun, Naruko-kun...

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.430
Take care of Sakamichi for me.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.000
Sakamichi...

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:11.610
Be careful, and keep riding your bike.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:14.110
Okay.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.770
I'm off!

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.050
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.090
I can hardly believe it rained yesterday.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.000
The weather's so nice.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:01.590
<i>RIDE.01  The Last Minegayama</i>

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:05.030
Hey.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.760
Good morning, Imaizumi-kun.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.920
You're right on time for opening.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.010
Did you take the bus today?

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:10.900
Yeah.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.470
This place is pretty far from the bus stop.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.430
But you'd do anything for love, right?

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.860
What do you mean by love?

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:20.860
Is it ready?

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.560
Hey.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.120
Hey, Kanzaki-san.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.240
It's ready.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.660
Your last one broke during the Inter-High.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.750
It's got a new frame.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.380
I stuck new components and wheels on it, too.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:39.880
It's your new bike.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.340
<i>Incredible.</i>

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.330
<i>It's so direct.</i>

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:47.060
<i>It's like the bike is responding to 
my legs' movements without any error.</i>

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:48.800
<i>And it's light, too.</i>

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.730
<i>I'm already at 40 kph, 
but it can go even faster.</i>

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.480
This time I made the 
components electric, too.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.230
Electric?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.710
The wires you've used to physically shift 
gears until now have been switched out

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.410
<b>Electric Signal</b>

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.410
<b>Cord</b>

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.410
<b>Motor</b>

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.410
<b>Motor</b>

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.410
<b>F Derailleur</b>

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.410
<b>R Derailleur</b>

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.410
<b>Battery</b>

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.690
for electric signals sent to 
motors that do it for you.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.410
It's like shifting gears using a switch.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:10.620
On this battery, you'll be able 
to ride about 1,500 kilometers.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.000
It's not that one's better than the other,

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:18.000
but you're the type to manage your 
body by shifting gears a lot.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.880
Even when you're pushed to your limit, 
you'll be able to accurately shift gears.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.470
This'll be a huge advantage for you.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:29.090
<i>There's zero delay when shifting gears.</i>

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.970
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:35.480
<i>It feels so strange to have the 
gear shift at the lightest touch.</i>

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.120
<i>But this bike can move!</i>

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.360
<i>It feels awesome.</i>

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.860
<i>Thank you, Kanzaki-san.</i>

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.110
<i>Kinjou-san...</i>

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:49.320
<i>I had a range of experiences 
at the Inter-High.</i>

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:56.300
<i>What I've felt since it ended is that 
I've definitely become stronger.</i>

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:59.290
<i>I'll become even stronger.</i>

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.090
<i>I'll go to the Inter-High again next year.</i>

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.800
<i>I'll kick aside the strong riders who 
will gather from all over the country.</i>

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:08.580
<i>I will, as Sohoku's ace!</i>

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:13.290
Um, hello.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.850
Welcome, Onoda-kun.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:20.650
H-Hello. Um, Kanzaki-san asked me to come.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.770
Yeah, I heard. Come in.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:26.650
Hey.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:31.410
Hello. Thanks for all your 
help at the Inter-High.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:34.160
What did you want to talk about?

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:41.230
The chromoly frame out front's the one 
you rode in the Inter-High, right?

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.850
Oh, yes. Thank you.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:44.710
Thanks to you, I...

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:45.960
Give it back.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:46.890
What?

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:53.890
What? I know I've been 
borrowing it from you, but...

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.780
But...

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:04.860
Ride this instead.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.810
It's a carbon module cast.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:11.600
The frame's made entirely from carbon fiber.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:15.330
It weighs half as much as the 
chromoly frame you've been riding.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.790
<i>Half?</i>

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.870
Even I can lift it easily.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.840
Weight is key for climbers.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:26.090
Take the next step forward, Onoda.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.050
<i>Forward...</i>

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:32.290
That bike will be able to meet your needs.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:34.980
<i>What is this?</i>

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:37.210
<i>It's so light.</i>

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.960
<i>I feel like I'm floating 
three centimeters above the ground.</i>

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.810
<i>It's so fast.</i>

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:46.220
This bike moves easily, far, and quickly.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.400
You can really pedal when you need to.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.200
It's the right bike for you.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:53.200
<i>The pedals really do turn fast.</i>

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:58.110
<i>I might even be able to pedal faster 
than I did at the Inter-High.</i>

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.450
Imaizumi-kun! Naruko-kun!

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:05.710
Onoda!

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:05.710
Onoda-kun!

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.780
What's your new weapon?

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.380
Kanzaki-san just gave it to me.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:14.220
A yellow carbon frame, huh?

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.720
Pretty flashy and cool.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:19.480
How's the new bike?

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.470
G-Good!

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:24.880
Since the way you ride heavy bikes is 
different from how you ride light bikes,

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.930
it'll take some getting used to.

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:30.690
But Kanzaki-san said once I get used 
to it, I'll be dramatically faster.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:37.990
Hotshot's got a new frame and electric
components, and Onoda-kun's got a new bike?

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.580
Looks like we had the same idea.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:45.000
What?

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.800
<i>What is this sound? Is that the wind?</i>

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.340
They're thick and huge. What are those?

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.180
On hills, the lightness of 
your wheels is important.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:58.510
I think Makishima-san said that.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:02.640
On flats, your wheel's wind 
resistance is important.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:06.730
They negate the wind blowing toward 
you and convert it into thrust.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.110
These are the ultimate wheels for sprinters...

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.980
Carbon deep-rimmed wheels!

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.990
Amazing.

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:17.290
Why don't the three of us 
go for a shakedown ride, then?

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.200
Try to keep up, Naruko.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.690
Shut up. I'll be leading the group.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.450
I'll show you just how fast my new weapon is.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:27.710
Ready, and...

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.340
Wait!

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.470
<b>Library</b>

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:44.430
Yeah. I know, Bro.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:47.060
I've packed most of my things.

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:52.040
I'll be fine. I'll talk to them, too.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.220
Yeah, bye.

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:08.930
<i>The Sohoku High Bicycle 
Racing Club was a good team.</i>

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:13.300
<i>But now it's time to say goodbye.</i>

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:15.360
<b>Club Withdrawal</b>

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:15.360
<b>Makishima Yusuke</b>

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:15.360
<b>Bicycle Racing Club</b>

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.180
<b>Club Withdrawal</b>

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:42.830
Why do I look so dejected?

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.620
We finally won the Inter-High.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.500
I should be leaving with a smile.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.000
<b>Inter-High Road Race
Boys' Champions</b>

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.630
<b>Idiot</b>

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.130
Why'd you write "idiot" on it?!

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:13.230
<b>Climber for life
Makishima Yusuk</b>

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:19.860
Time for one last climb up Minegayama.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.670
What do you want, old man?

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:31.580
I'm not slacking off just 
because it's summer break.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:35.670
What? I'm training with hotshot right now.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.880
Huh? Onoda-kun's off training by himself.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.380
What?

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.680
Makishima-san is?

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.980
Yeah, I heard he was going to college.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.720
But why's he going overseas?

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:53.490
His brother's living in England by himself.

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:57.030
He's going to help him 
while living abroad there.

00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:58.940
<i>No one told me anything about that!</i>

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:00.300
No one told me, either.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:02.530
We just heard the news, too.

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:05.620
Their school year starts 
in September over there.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.080
<i>September? You mean this September?</i>

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.210
Yeah.

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:13.780
I did think he was spending a lot of time 
in the library since the Inter-High ended.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:16.960
Apparently, he was finishing all 
his credits here ahead of schedule

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:19.620
so he could go to college there.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:20.670
<i>What?</i>

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.250
Are you serious?

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:26.180
What about the race to send 
off the third-years, then?

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.090
What about his bike?

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:36.770
Makishima-san!

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.770
Are you on your way to practice now?

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.000
That bike seems to be working out well.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.070
It's a good fit for you.

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:52.610
Oh, I'm not nearly good enough for it yet.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.430
I haven't tapped into my full potential yet.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:58.490
I still have old habits to shake.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:06.260
Imagine sliding your feet forward when your 
toes are applying torque to the crank.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.260
You'll move farther on a 
lighter frame that way.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:12.300
Slide my feet?

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.960
Oh, I see.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:18.230
Thank you. I'll give it a try.

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:31.530
Onoda, I'm on my way up Minegayama.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.120
Want to join me?

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:43.640
I just came back from Minegayama.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:46.860
Would it be all right 
if we rode another time?

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.470
Yeah.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:09.280
Actually, can I come with you after all?

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:13.950
I got a strange feeling in my chest.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.750
Let's go up Minegayama together.

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:18.460
<i>This kid...</i>

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.980
<i>I can't tell if he's slow or sharp.</i>

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.610
Yeah, let's go!

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.260
You've gotten faster.

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:40.900
Yeah. Um, Makishima-san, you're cool, too.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:45.940
"Scary" is good enough for me.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.530
Sakamichi!

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:49.490
Yes, sir!

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.010
Hey, Sakamichi!

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.100
Yes, sir!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:05.180
Do you enjoy riding your bike?

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.250
Yes!

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:19.900
Lately, I've been talking with Naruko-kun 
and Imaizumi-kun about how we'll

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:23.420
"surpass the third-years 
by the time they graduate."

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.210
That sounded just like him.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.070
What? Really?

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.710
You beat me again at the end today,

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:34.700
but I'm hoping to get stronger 
by the time you graduate.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.300
At least, I hope I do.

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:42.000
Will you race me again then?

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:49.500
I'm always riding with you.

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:52.780
When you think of it that way,
we can race anytime.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:58.940
On zigzagging climbs, on straight 
roads that stretch on forever,

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:01.730
on overgrown country roads...

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:08.190
Next year and the year after,
I'll always be riding in front of you.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:10.760
So pass me.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.130
Become stronger.

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:23.240
We're counting on you to 
carry our Sohoku, Sakamichi.

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.500
Makishima-san...

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:36.840
I'm happy to have served as your captain.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:41.100
You endured hard practices 
and rode well at races.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:45.050
I'm truly grateful to all of you.

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:45.950
Thank you.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:48.650
It was nothing.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.150
Same goes to you, Captain.

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.320
Thank you!

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:57.380
We really are blessed.

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:59.260
I had an awesome time.

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:00.580
Teshima...

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.660
Yes, sir.

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:06.500
You're the next captain of the 
Sohoku Bicycle Racing Club.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.930
Second-year, Teshima Junta!

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:09.790
Yes, sir!

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.130
Aoyagi Hajime!

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:11.920
Yes, sir.

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:13.510
You're the vice-captain.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.600
Yes, sir.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.840
The rest is up to you guys.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:18.410
Ride.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.050
Fight for every second.

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:23.810
Next year's Inter-High has already begun.

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:25.000
Yes, sir!

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:34.430
Sohoku won. We beat reigning 
champions, Hakone Academy.

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:36.280
And at the same time, we became burdened...

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:40.690
...with the weight, responsibility,
and pressure of being the winning team

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:43.160
of the Inter-High.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.880
At the next Inter-High—no,

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:50.300
starting with our next race,
the other teams will be gunning for us.

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:53.210
We must leap past them and win again.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:56.690
No matter the circumstances.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:18:04.220
After all, at the next Inter-High, 
we'll be riding with single-digit tags...

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.650
Because we are the champions.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:14.480
Come. Let me see how much stronger 
you became during the Inter-High.

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.100
<i>Let me see?</i>

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.610
Interesting. Does this 
mean a race, perm guy?

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:20.950
Didn't you hear me?

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.710
That's what I said.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:26.080
To the traffic signal at the 
end of this 15-kilometer flat.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.500
Let's race!

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:30.590
<i>He accelerated.</i>

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:32.380
<i>Is he trying to pull ahead here?</i>

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.900
<i>No, Teshima-san is a strategist.</i>

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:38.800
<i>He could be plotting to make us wear 
out our legs by chasing after him.</i>

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:47.390
<i>The quiet one jumped ahead.</i>

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.550
<i>Their switch was ultra smooth.</i>

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:51.810
<i>Their teamwork is still going strong.</i>

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:52.610
<i>No...</i>

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:53.780
Naruko!

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:54.640
Yeah!

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:58.780
They're trying to pull ahead 
of us with brute force!

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:02.530
<i>They knew we'd expect them to 
strategize since they're not strong,</i>

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:05.240
<i>so they did the opposite.</i>

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.150
Let's accelerate at full speed!

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:07.750
I know!

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:09.750
Can we close this gap?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.500
We will catch them!

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:16.370
<i>I must be stupid. I didn't notice.</i>

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:17.800
<i>I didn't even pay any attention to it.</i>

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.630
<i>Now that I get a closer look, their legs...</i>

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:23.210
<i>Their legs are nothing like 
they were at the training camp!</i>

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:25.350
<i>Those are the legs of someone 
who's practiced a ton!</i>

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.660
Will the first-years catch them?

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.080
I'm not so sure.

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:38.150
While they were looking 
toward the Inter-High,

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:41.710
Teshima and Aoyagi never stopped practicing.

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:43.780
And they've gotten stronger.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.420
Especially Aoyagi.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:51.500
His abilities as a sprinter are blossoming.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:54.710
Aoyagi...

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:56.960
What percent are you at right now?

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.750
70%.

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:03.430
Then let's go to 100% for the last two 
kilometers and pull ahead of them.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.590
Got it.

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:21.730
What's wrong, Naruko?

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:24.860
Are those deep-rimmed wheels just for show?

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:31.160
Imaizumi, don't think 
you'll be the ace forever.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:34.080
You're not strong enough yet.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.180
We will—Sohoku will become even stronger!

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.210
We are the second generation of Sohoku!

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:40.620
Yes, sir!

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:47.290
Looks like the second-years won.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:50.670
Check it out. They look frustrated.

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:53.310
Thinking they were better

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:57.150
for even a moment let their biggest 
chance slip away from them.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.650
That's part of road racing, too.

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:00.980
But...

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:04.780
I'm most worried about him.

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:06.680
Onoda...

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:11.160
<i>I can't catch up. I can't catch up...</i>

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.410
<i>I need to work harder.</i>

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:17.930
I can't be weak. I can't be weak.

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:26.020
<i>I can't be weak...</i>

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:33.060
<i>Makishima-san...</i>

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:34.660
Become stronger.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:41.850
<i>How can I become stronger?</i>

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:26.840
It's tea time.

00:23:29.100 --> 00:23:29.910
Junta.

00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:32.040
I almost forgot.

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:40.520
<i>NEXT RIDE  What Makishima Left Behind</i>

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:45.520
